In `LoggerWithConfig`, a nil `config.Output` is never left nil: the defaults block sets it to `DefaultLoggerConfig.Output` (middleware/logger.go:95-97), and since `DefaultLoggerConfig` doesn't set `Output`, it stays nil. So at write time the fallback branch runs (lines 215-218):

    if config.Output == nil {
        _, err = c.Logger().Output().Write(buf.Bytes())
        return
    }

i.e. the log line is written to the current request's Echo logger output, `c.Logger().Output()` — the `echo.Logger` of the `Echo` instance (default `log.New("echo")`, whose output is `os.Stdout`), not to the middleware's own config output. That matches the doc comment "Optional. Default value os.Stdout."

