It returns the number of bytes just read together with `echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge` (a 413 HTTPError) as the error:

    func (r *limitedReader) Read(b []byte) (n int, err error) {
        n, err = r.reader.Read(b)
        r.read += int64(n)
        if r.read > r.limit {
            return n, echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge
        }
        return
    }

So once the cumulative `r.read` exceeds `config.limit`, every further read returns `(n, echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge)`; the underlying read error is discarded in that case.

`DefaultBodyDumpConfig.Skipper` is `DefaultSkipper` (middleware/body_dump.go:36-38), i.e. the function in middleware/middleware.go:

    // DefaultSkipper returns false which processes the middleware.
    func DefaultSkipper(echo.Context) bool {
        return false
    }

So by default no request is skipped — the BodyDump middleware always runs.

